# seed/MANIFEST -- unity order of the seed compiler (R0). Owner: contracts.
#
# FORMAT: one repo-relative path per line; '#' starts a comment line; blank lines are ignored.
#   The unity source is the concatenation of the listed files in this order, each followed by one "\n"
#   (scripts/seed/build.sh writes build/seed/seed-unity.kotoba). A listed file that does not exist yet is
#   skipped with a warning by unit.sh and is a hard error for build.sh.
#
# NAMESPACE: exactly one (ns seed (:export [main])), in 00-ns.kotoba. No other file has an ns form.
#
# MODULE PREFIX RULE: every top-level name defined in a module starts with that module's prefix (column 2
#   below), e.g. 10-lex defines lx-run, lx-scan-int ... Exceptions: 00-ns defines the generated UPPER-CASE
#   constants and `main`; 99-entry defines `seed-main`. Tests (seed/tests/unit/<mod>_t.kotoba) prefix their
#   own helpers with `t-` and define `seed-main`. A module may CALL any name of a module listed BEFORE it;
#   calls to a LATER module are only allowed from 90-drv and 99-entry (unit tests would not link otherwise).
#   Every function is defn- except main (MEMORY-MAP rule L3).
#
# UNIT ASSEMBLY (scripts/seed/unit.sh <mod>): 00-ns, then the base modules 01-mem 02-io that precede <mod>,
#   then the modules named on the test's `;; deps: <mod> <mod> ...` line (in MANIFEST order), then <mod>,
#   then seed/tests/unit/<mod>_t.kotoba. 99-entry is never part of a unit build.
#
# path                    prefix   owner (design section 4.2)
seed/00-ns.kotoba
#                         (none)   contracts: ns form, GENERATED constants, `main` -> (seed-main)
seed/01-mem.kotoba
#                         mem-     01-mem: mem-new, mem-alloc, mem-hash, mem-u2dec, byte-buffer helpers
seed/02-io.kotoba
#                         io-      02-io: io-read-file, io-argc, io-arg, io-write-bytes, io-err, io-out
seed/10-lex.kotoba
#                         lx-      10-lex: lx-run
seed/11-read.kotoba
#                         rd-      11-read: rd-run
seed/12-kirread.kotoba
#                         kr-      12-kirread (agent KIR, 2026-10-02): kr-lex, kr-run -- KIR text -> Seed-0 read tree
seed/20-names.kotoba
#                         nm-      20-names: nm-run, nm-intern, scope API
seed/21-check.kotoba
#                         ck-      21-check: ck-run
seed/30-lower.kotoba
#                         lw-      30-lower: lw-run (+ lw-interp, test-only but in the unity file)
seed/40-a64enc.kotoba
#                         enc-     40-a64enc: pure encoders
seed/41-a64gen.kotoba
#                         gn-      41-a64gen: gn-run
seed/42-layout.kotoba
#                         ly-      42-layout: ly-run
seed/50-out.kotoba
#                         out-     50-out: out-write, out-extract
seed/90-drv.kotoba
#                         drv-     driver (contracts owner): drv-main, drv-check, drv-compile, drv-extract
seed/99-entry.kotoba
#                         seed-    `seed-main` -> (drv-main). Last; replaced by the test's seed-main in unit builds
